
  [1mError handling[0m

  Tracking must never break login. [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m throws in real conditions — disabled in private mode ([38;5;153mSecurityError[39m),
  full ([38;5;153mQuotaExceededError[39m) — so every storage operation is wrapped; on failure it warns to console and returns. A
  failed [38;5;153mtrack()[39m is not a failed login. Corrupt or non-array JSON under the key is treated as empty rather than thrown.

  [1mConsequence of the ES-module choice[0m

  [38;5;153mfile://[39m will no longer load the page — module scripts require an origin. You'll need to serve it ([38;5;153mpython3 -m [39m
  [38;5;153mhttp.server[39m, [38;5;153mnpx serve[39m, anything). Flagging it because opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m from disk works today and will stop working.

  [1mFiles touched[0m

  New [38;5;153mtracker.js[39m; modified [38;5;153mapp.js[39m and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m; [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m only if you want tooling.

  [1mTooling[0m

  The repo has no test runner, no linter, no formatter. This is the cheapest moment to add them, and
  [38;5;153mtrack[39m/storage-failure behavior is genuinely worth testing.
